From 162ea1f6eb4342778fb874b7c956439332488d2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 14:57:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v3.1.8: the firewall walker becomes advisory, System
 Information rebuilt, vendor WLCSM blobs

Firewall table walker (reaper_fwsim) v1.1 -> v1.5, three passes on field data
  Two reports on v3.1.7's Rule Status shared one cause: a synthetic witness
  address that a live SOURCE list happens to select tests the address, not
  the feature. Both firewalls were fine; the walker was wrong on every red
  but one.
  - wansrc_pick(): the WAN-side witness source is probed against every
    source-side set and the first unclaimed candidate wins (198.51.100.7 was
    itself inside a threat feed's bogon range). A fully claimed set is an
    honest red with a note, never a bypass. IPv6 twin (wan6src), and
    lanhost_pick() for an allowlist-aware LAN host.
  - E8b gated like rc/rwarden.c do_out (dir out|both); inbound-only witnesses
    are absent from filter/RW_OUT rather than red.
  - E1/E2/E3 could never fire in the field: they read nvram
    reaper_fwsim_banned, which nothing in the tree ever wrote. They now read
    Warden's own ban list (rw_list_get); the key stays an override.
  - ADVISORY BY DESIGN: the walker is passive and informative, never
    authoritative. rwatch 3g never FAILs on a red witness (one advisory line
    per change of the red set); reaper_diag 14g is INFO; rmcpd describes it
    as advisory; the rail badge is gone and the shell no longer polls;
    the dashboard tag reads Advisory; the Firewall page count is uncoloured
    under an RFW_320 banner. mode=advisory is a constant, not a switch.
  - Model review, every connection class: multicast 224/4 is local; ICMP and
    ICMPv6 type NAMES with `!` are honoured (the negation was dropped and v6
    echo-request mapped to 8, so stock default_block would have false-redded
    ping rows); dual WAN uses the primary unit; DHCP sport 68/546; the admin
    allowlist gates the WAN web/SSH rows; DMZ -> A4/A4b note + B6; a linked
    SDN -> G1 note; a proto-name table (ipv6-crypt and friends) so a named
    protocol is not "unmodelled"; an unmodelled match with an INERT target
    (TCPMSS) continues instead of deferring; per-field deferred mark doubt;
    D2 = the emitter's truth (DROP); D5 = NOTE under an admin allowlist.
  - False-green rows added: A4b (a router-address high port must not be
    translated), H7 (INVALID WAN->LAN rests on policy: stock's FORWARD
    INVALID drop is commented out in firewall.c), H7b (INVALID WAN->router).
    D3b labelled (L3); H6 names bridge-local.
  - C7: a set-keyed policy-routing selector (-m set --match-set rwfw_<n> dst)
    resolves its members at run time, so its mark is not witnessed - NOTE
    n/a, the reasoning F1 already applies to fqdn/geo. -s and MAC rows keep
    a positive and a negative each.
  Host suite 121 -> 214 checks plus 23 advisory-posture checks. Metal: 104
  rows, 95 green / 0 red / 0 depends / 9 n/a in 0.44 s on the RT-BE96U.

System Information, native (www/Reaper_Sysinfo.asp)
  The same data as stock Tools_Sysinfo.asp, regrouped by the question being
  asked rather than by data source. No new backend: it reads
  /ajax_sysinfo.asp, /ajax_coretmp.asp and /cpu_ram_status.asp and PARSES
  them, where stock executed the response as script. Band labels come from
  wlX_nband, not a hardcoded model switch. 42 RSYS_* tokens in all 25 packs.
  Wired from the rail and both menuTrees; the stock page is retired behind
  the SUP redirect in reaper_inject.c and left byte-pristine.

WLCSM netlink socket leak ("stuck nvram"): the vendor's fix, as shipped
  ASUS stock 9.0.0.6.102_42015 carries the fix in two closed blobs and
  nowhere in source: libnvram.so (_wlcsm_init closes its fds on re-init,
  the port candidate gets its own field instead of aliasing the saved PID,
  error-path cleanup) and libwlcsm.so (a bounded, backed-off retry in
  wlcsm_nvram_getall). Both are swapped into
  router-sysdep.rt-be96u/{wlan/nvram,wlcsm}/prebuilt/ from the vendor's own
  image - a blob SWAP with recorded provenance, never a binary patch.
  wlcsm_agent is defined by one and imported by the other: they travel
  together. All six models ship the identical pair; the siblings take it on
  their own branches and CI takes it from overlays/wlcsm-42015-blobs.tar.gz.
  The wlcsm_bindfix LD_PRELOAD shim is retired: start_wlcsm_bindfix() is
  inert (removes a leftover /etc/ld.so.preload, ignores its nvram key, logs
  once), the .so is no longer built, and the Tools > Other Settings toggle
  is gone. rwatch's hung-nvram reaper stays as the safety net.

Also: 25 dictionaries in lockstep (RSYS_*, RFW_319/320, RFW_292 reworded).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
